> npm test && npm run typecheck


> pi-model-discoverer@0.1.0 test
> tsx --test test/*.test.ts

✔ applyModelOverride creates modelOverrides and preserves other provider fields (1.686834ms)
✔ applyModelOverride merges into existing overrides without dropping siblings (0.274667ms)
✔ null removes keys and prunes empty override containers (0.187708ms)
✔ undefined patch keys leave existing values untouched (0.228458ms)
✔ applyModelOverride rejects unknown providers, malformed json, and non-object nodes (2.948917ms)
✔ models.json parsing honors discoverModels opt-in, comments, and trailing commas (1.858583ms)
✔ normalization deduplicates, preserves explicit metadata, modelApis, and conservative defaults (0.339333ms)
✔ discovery sends the resolved credential only to the configured origin with redirects blocked (18.722125ms)
✔ Anthropic catalogs use x-api-key and paginate without following server URLs (0.681334ms)
✔ failures never expose response bodies, URLs, or credential-bearing errors (3.008625ms)
✔ malformed saved keys cannot escape through header validation errors (0.643791ms)
✔ cancellation does not issue a request (0.178416ms)
✔ refresh hook restores persisted catalogs offline and persists new ones after fetch (0.62075ms)
✔ Pi's actual extension loader registers the command and discovery hook from models.json (40.619042ms)
✔ loader tolerates a missing models.json (3.582083ms)
✔ native discovery delegates to Pi, selecting only authenticated dynamic providers (1.960416ms)
✔ session-start refresh does not force a network fetch (0.192209ms)
✔ explicit unknown and unauthenticated providers do not cause a refresh (0.219917ms)
✔ refresh reports per-provider failures without leaking native auth errors (0.257ms)
✔ cancelled refresh is not reported as successful (0.170333ms)
✔ a silently superseded refresh does not claim that new models were published (0.186ms)
